;;; Written for this review: why `ein render kb` of x2b.ein draws no
;;; (confused Ann). Two programs in one comparison: this one names the rule
;;; `confused`, like the relation it concludes (as x2b.ein does), and its twin
;;; kbview-rule-named-apart.ein names it `c`. Both hold (confused Ann) at root.

(person Ann)
(think Ann (false))
(rule confused () :match (think ?p (false)) :assert (confused ?p) :why "c")
